  advocacy: {
    MY:{args:[
      ["Malaysia ratified the ILO forced labor protocol in 2022 and made forced labor an offence in the Employment Act in 2023. Passport retention, debt from recruitment fees and the tie to one employer are among the ILO forced labor indicators and can be put to the ILO supervisory bodies.","Malaysia meratifikasi protokol kerja paksa ILO pada 2022 dan menjadikan kerja paksa tindak pidana dalam Akta Kerja pada 2023. Penahanan paspor, utang dari biaya rekrutmen dan keterikatan pada satu majikan termasuk indikator kerja paksa ILO dan bisa diajukan ke badan pengawas ILO."],
      ["The exclusion of domestic workers from the minimum wage and from Part XII rests on the First Schedule, not on the statute's purpose; the 2022 memorandum with Indonesia already accepts a wage and cost rules that domestic law could adopt.","Pengecualian PRT dari upah minimum dan Bagian XII bersandar pada Jadual Pertama, bukan tujuan undang-undang; nota kesepahaman 2022 dengan Indonesia sudah menerima upah dan aturan biaya yang bisa diadopsi hukum domestik."]],
     avenues:[
      ["Claims to the Labour Court under s. 69 of the Employment Act, which is open to foreign workers with a valid pass.","Tuntutan ke Mahkamah Buruh menurut s. 69 Akta Kerja, terbuka bagi pekerja asing dengan pas yang sah."],
      ["Complaints to SUHAKAM, Malaysia's national human rights institution.","Pengaduan ke SUHAKAM, lembaga HAM nasional Malaysia."],
      ["Comments by workers' organizations to the ILO on C29 and P29.","Komentar organisasi pekerja kepada ILO tentang C29 dan P29."]]},
    SG:{args:[
      ["Domestic workers sit outside the Employment Act and have no limit on hours; the 2013 and 2023 rest-day rules show that the work pass conditions can carry labor standards, which can be extended.","PRT berada di luar Akta Kerja dan tanpa batas jam kerja; aturan hari istirahat 2013 dan 2023 menunjukkan bahwa syarat izin kerja bisa memuat standar ketenagakerjaan, yang bisa diperluas."],
      ["Singapore is a party to ILO C29 and the Palermo Protocol; the tie to one employer and the employer's power to cancel the permit can be examined against the ILO forced labor indicators.","Singapura pihak ILO C29 dan Protokol Palermo; keterikatan pada satu majikan dan wewenang majikan membatalkan izin bisa diuji terhadap indikator kerja paksa ILO."]],
     avenues:[
      ["Salary claims through TADM mediation and the Employment Claims Tribunals, during which a worker may stay on a special pass.","Tuntutan upah melalui mediasi TADM dan Employment Claims Tribunals; selama proses, pekerja bisa tinggal dengan pas khusus."],
      ["Help from the Migrant Workers' Centre or the Centre for Domestic Employees.","Bantuan dari Migrant Workers' Centre atau Centre for Domestic Employees."]]},
    TH:{args:[
      ["Thailand is a party to ILO C188 and P29 and to both UN covenants. The bar on migrants founding or leading unions can be raised under ICCPR Art. 22 and ICESCR Art. 8, and in ILO reviews even though Thailand has not ratified C87.","Thailand pihak ILO C188 dan P29 serta kedua kovenan PBB. Larangan bagi migran mendirikan atau memimpin serikat bisa diajukan menurut Pasal 22 ICCPR dan Pasal 8 ICESCR, serta dalam peninjauan ILO meski Thailand belum meratifikasi C87."],
      ["Farm workers employed seasonally are outside the Social Security Act; this can be framed as indirect discrimination under ICESCR Art. 9.","Buruh tani musiman berada di luar UU Jaminan Sosial; ini bisa dibingkai sebagai diskriminasi tidak langsung menurut Pasal 9 ICESCR."]],
     avenues:[
      ["Hotlines 1694 and 1546, and labor inspectors; for fishers, Port-in Port-out centers.","Saluran 1694 dan 1546, serta pengawas ketenagakerjaan; bagi nelayan, pusat Port-in Port-out."],
      ["Labor court claims, which are free of court fees.","Gugatan di pengadilan perburuhan, tanpa biaya perkara."],
      ["Complaints to the National Human Rights Commission of Thailand.","Pengaduan ke Komnas HAM Thailand."]]},
    BN:{args:[
      ["Brunei has no general minimum wage for the sectors where most migrants work and is party to few ILO conventions; ILO membership since 2007 still brings the 1998 Declaration on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work into play.","Brunei tidak memiliki upah minimum umum untuk sektor tempat kebanyakan migran bekerja dan baru menjadi pihak sedikit konvensi ILO; keanggotaan ILO sejak 2007 tetap membawa Deklarasi 1998 tentang Prinsip dan Hak Mendasar di Tempat Kerja."]],
     avenues:[
      ["Complaints to the Department of Labour.","Pengaduan ke Departemen Tenaga Kerja."],
      ["Help from the embassy of the worker's country.","Bantuan dari kedutaan negara asal pekerja."]]}
  },

